# Line endings.
#
# Git converts to CRLF on Windows checkouts by default. That is harmless for
# most files here, but not for anything Linux executes: a shell script with
# carriage returns fails on the first line that matters --
#
#     setup-node.sh: line 15: $'\r': command not found
#     setup-node.sh: line 16: set: pipefail: invalid option name
#
# which silently disables the script's own error handling and then continues.
# The committed blobs were already LF; the damage happened on checkout, and the
# dev server serves the working copy straight to contributors.
#
# So the files that end up running inside a container are pinned to LF on every
# platform. Everything else keeps git's normal behaviour.

*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
